course: dictionary
lesson: 6542
title: Reading a word in its setting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A newbie is someone who is new to something and does not know much yet. You might hear it in games, online forums, clubs and everyday chat. To be sure what it means, read the words around it.
explain: At drama club, a girl says loudly «Ugh, newbie» and rolls her eyes. The loud "Ugh" and the eye-roll show she is annoyed or teasing, so this is not a friendly welcome. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Someone new who does not know much yet.
explain: Newbie can also be said in a kind way. The phrase help the newbies means show new people how things work. The same word can sound friendly or a bit teasing, so the tone and actions around it give the clue.
fact: A newbie is someone who is new to something and does not know much yet.
fact: Newbie is slang, so people use it in casual talk rather than formal writing.
fact: A newbie can be new to a game, a club, a job or a website.
fact: «A total newbie» means someone who is completely new to something.
fact: Newbies can be teased or helped, and the way people say it shows which.
exercise: «Ugh, newbie» is said loudly with an eye-roll. What does newbie mean here? | A famous player who is the best at the game | *Someone who is new and does not know much yet | Someone who is very old | A helpful teacher who runs the club
exercise: Jayden says «help the newbies». What does he want? | Ignore the new people completely | *Show new people how things work | Make the new people leave the club | Give the new people a prize for winning
exercise: Lily says, «I'm a total newbie at chess.» What does she mean? | *She is completely new to chess | She is the best chess player in the school | She does not like games at all | She has played chess for many years
test:
What does the eye-roll suggest about the girl who says «Ugh, newbie»? | *Annoyance or teasing | Excitement about meeting a new friend | Sleepiness after a long day | Surprise at a magic trick
test:
Which is the best meaning of newbie? | A person who has been doing something for years | *A person who is new to something and does not know much yet | A type of computer game | A friendly teacher who runs a club
exam:
Which sentence uses newbie in a friendly way? | *We should help the newbies learn the rules | Ugh, newbie, go away | Newbie is a very long word | He ate a newbie for lunch
